    "BYTE-identical BODY10 callback is reused: event0x1002 only, volatile raw flagbyte27 read, nonzero gate, original int/unsigned-long varargs and exact printer format. It forms no Rust reference to the mutable descriptor. Existing C flag-update/exclusion and kprintf contracts remain; no new synchronization promise is introduced.",
    "Selected C branch is extern-only when both existing logger selection and new storage flag are enabled. Disabling storage retains the exact BODY10 C global record; disabling logger retains original C body/dkprintf LOCAL descriptor. New CMake cfg/module/source and C storage selection are paired inside the existing supported branch. Logical fallback line665 and outer line672 restore remain unchanged.",
    "Actual C oracle retains genuine dkprintf and original function identifier with HOST-only asm alias and filename/line remap. C extern consumer uses genuine headers and static ABI assertions, takes the actual Rust descriptor address, and writes/reads the real C bitfield. The oracle LOCAL descriptor is independent from the one GLOBAL selected Rust record.",
    "Fixture qualification exercises3750 original C/Rust pairs over six events, five flag bytes, five CPU ints, five unsigned-long values and five printer returns. It compares an independent expected trace and rendered text, metadata/line/padding canaries, C/Rust pointer identity and bidirectional flagbyte/C-bitfield roundtrips. Source/authenticated retained stdout confirms1 test passed0 failed; no execution was repeated.",
    "Independent read-only ELF parser inspection of real Rust object, C consumer, C oracle, partial link and final HOST fixture confirms one GLOBAL OBJECT32 target aligned8 in writable alloc __verbose; C consumer/oracle target symbols are undefined imports. Original oracle contributes one distinct LOCAL32 record; partial/final HOST have exactly those two record symbols. No Rust-object constructor section exists.",
    "All39 frozen source/actual-source bindings, genuine header/type providers, qualification/result/ELF references, raw four STARTED/JOINED/stdout/stderr records and all nine canonical118 postimages were authenticated. Four recorded argv/cwd equal the exact plan; each PID/birth has direct wait4 exit0, whole-group absence and closed streams; stderr is empty. No retries or failures in this BODY11 HOST run."
